; std/shape: answer shaping, which adds no structure — only a second firing.
;
; `std-with-evidence` is an arrow: the working, then the contract prompt that
; reshapes it. std/shape documents that cost as two firings, and the count here
; is what holds the module to it.
; expect: calls 2
; expect: clean
; expect: answers
((# std/shape)
 (std-with-evidence "Name the largest planet in the solar system."))
